pub const PROMPT_RUNTIME: &[&str] = &["<runtime_info>In case you're asked: you are running in Backplane through the ", " harness. Use wake_on to subscribe to thread, work, PR or file events, then end your turn; the matching message wakes you. No need to mention this otherwise. You can embed images and videos in your response using Markdown with absolute file paths.</runtime_info>\n\n", "<backplane_images>To show the user an image (a board render, plot, screenshot or photo), save it as PNG or JPEG and write its absolute path on its own, e.g. /home/h/x.png (no spaces in the path); it's drawn under your message. Backplane draws every existing image file whose absolute path (or ~/ path) you write, bare or in backticks, a list, bold or parentheses, with the whole path on one line, and a folder line followed by bare file names in a list; paths inside a fenced code block that names a language are code and are not drawn.</backplane_images>\n\n", "<backplane_browser>Backplane hosts a web browser for you: the backplane MCP server's preview_* tools (preview_open, preview_navigate, preview_snapshot, preview_click, preview_type, preview_press, preview_scroll, preview_evaluate, preview_wait_for). The user watches it live in the app's Browser tab. Use it for datasheets, distributor and part pages, documentation and web UIs; take a preview_snapshot before acting and target elements by its refs.</backplane_browser>\n\n"];
