pub const PROMPT_KICAD_FORK: &[&str] = &[" This is Backplane KiCad ", ", source commit ", ". Edit boards and schematics through the backplane MCP tool `kicad_ipc` {path, type, message}: Backplane runs one headless KiCad per project and sends your command to it over KiCad's IPC API (type is the protobuf command, e.g. `kiapi.board.commands.GetItems`; message is its fields as JSON; `kicad_ipc_status` shows the server, its version and the commands it has). Headless KiCad has no selection or view state: always pass explicit item IDs (KIIDs from GetItems), wrap edits in BeginCommit/EndCommit, then SaveDocument; unsaved work is undone with EndCommit CMA_DROP. Backplane KiCad bp.4 supports partial FootprintInstance updates and CreateItems with a symbol library id; symbol libraries load on demand, including for PlaceSymbolFromLibrary. If a runtime lacks `footprint-partial-update` or `symbol-from-libid`, the hub refuses the unsafe request and gives the workaround (send the full FootprintInstance, or use LoadAllLibraries + GetLibraryStatuses + PlaceSymbolFromLibrary). Always start the server through the runtime's `bin/kicad-cli` (Backplane does). Backplane's viewers follow the saved files. Read the matching guide https://github.com/BackplaneWorks/Backplane_KiCad/blob/", "/BACKPLANE_IPC.md (protocol definitions are under api/proto at that revision). ERC/DRC and exports stay on the CLI above. The SWIG `pcbnew` Python module no longer exists in this KiCad, so don't use it: edit through `kicad_ipc`. When `kicad_ipc` answers that IPC is unavailable, it says why and gives the fallback (edit the file directly or use the CLI, then re-read the file). Preserve any `<native-filename>.backplane.json` companion metadata when moving or saving project files."];
